                <p class="snippet" >
                     S.C.R 530; Ciarlariello v. Schacter, [1993] 2 S.C.R. 119; Egan and Nesbit v. Canada (1993), 153 N.R. 161; Brooks v. Canada Safeway Ltd., [1989] 1 S.C.R. 1219; <b>Janzen</b> v. Platy Enterprises Ltd., [1989] 1 S.C.R. 1252; R. v. Oakes, [1986] 1 S.C.R. 103; Malette v. Shulman (1990), 72 O.R. (2d) 417; Nancy B. v. Hôtel‐Dieu de &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;The fact that this is not a bar to a remedy under s. 15(1) seems to me to have been clearly decided by Brooks v. Canada Safeway Ltd., [1989] 1 S.C.R. 1219, and <b>Janzen</b> v. Platy Enterprises Ltd., [1989] 1 S.C.R. 1252. In Brooks, the question was whether unfavourable treatment on account of pregnancy could be regarded as sex &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;In <b>Janzen</b> this Court had to determine whether sexual harassment was a form of sex discrimination. 
